{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:34:34.165616Z","id":"f585f63eb035eabc9a041442847db6819b2b091091ac5b35bf07669c1e8c6e86","body":{"detail":"In docs/verification.md §10.2 and §10.3 (2026-10-09, d436b13 against main 527db6c, shared machine at load 16-30), the branch's subdomain comment ready read 101, 98 and 100 ms in the quality gate's quick run (limit 94 ms, scale 1.09; all three attempts failed), 97 ms on one of three solo reruns (limit 86; its retry read 81), 86 ms in the full `just perf` run (limit 86), and 81 and 83 ms otherwise. Main's build read 81, 83, 82 and 80 ms in the same interleaved runs. Every other time-to-usable measure matched main. The gate retries absorbed it in the solo reruns but not in the gate run. Whether something the branch records on the path a page takes to comment-ready (a viewer row, an audit insert, the journal appender's read) costs this, or it is load, is not settled: measure web/perf/usable.perf.ts subdomain comment ready on a quiet machine, branch against main, before merging.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1643},"end":{"line":1648},"content_hash":"d7d7999a2c1c93d287ddd23c909a4e8374ad6471e481c1f2e2c68db2057c588b"},"summary":"Time to usable's subdomain comment ready runs over its limit on this branch now and then, never on main","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:18:44.697444Z","id":"0ec2218948961006563d459cb637b8f29888a013b1d02a2737ff98c8334ca7bf","body":{"detail":"Measured on a home seeded by main (schema 21, 300 artifacts, 11,664 comments, 1,585 versions), upgraded with bf1180d: 16,715 backfilled events, about 650 B each in audit_events with its indexes and 1.3 KB each in the journal. Neither is pruned by default (journal_retain_days 0, the table kept indefinitely), and an agent in a wait loop adds a tool.call (and under Claude Code a tool.call_id) every wait.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"fad347bfe0932bf3c8bfbb95022fe5089f50de6fe7c9d3a8672f5812ae9b436b"},"suggested_fix":"State the measured cost in the contract and README where [toolpath] is documented, and offer journal_retain_days in the upgrade note; consider whether wait_for_feedback calls need a tool.call each.","summary":"Disk use on upgrade is several times the history: a 9.2 MB perf-seed home grew to 20 MB of database plus a 22 MB journal","tags":["review","disk","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:18:44.697640Z","id":"1e79ad8b9a4a72940e4b2846bce0f2538ed389266b6e4e50225d8d7d7792ad31","body":{"detail":"Between the link and comment mode the shell and bridge make only GET requests plus PUT looked, seen, presence and the stream POST, all in UNAUDITED (crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:719-764) and unchanged; web/shell differs from main only by type annotations (web/shell/src/api.ts), so the bundles are the same code. The only new background work during a sample is the journal appender's 1 s quiet tick, one indexed events_after read on a reader. A token publish now makes the CLI owner row, folded once by the first browser's token claim, which sample() does in its warm-up tab. Not measured on a quiet machine: the machine was loaded (load 7-15) and slept during this review.","kind":"comment","references":"f585f63eb035eabc9a041442847db6819b2b091091ac5b35bf07669c1e8c6e86","summary":"Traced the comment-ready path: nothing this branch records or changes runs on it","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620876Z","id":"bc7fce33479e73db5bd96776ad9010791c1289b29c828dfbc9db17630154323b","body":{"detail":"In docs/verification.md §10.2 and §10.3 (2026-10-09, d436b13 against main 527db6c, shared machine at load 16-30), the branch's subdomain comment ready read 101, 98 and 100 ms in the quality gate's quick run (limit 94 ms, scale 1.09; all three attempts failed), 97 ms on one of three solo reruns (limit 86; its retry read 81), 86 ms in the full `just perf` run (limit 86), and 81 and 83 ms otherwise. Main's build read 81, 83, 82 and 80 ms in the same interleaved runs. Every other time-to-usable measure matched main. The gate retries absorbed it in the solo reruns but not in the gate run. Whether something the branch records on the path a page takes to comment-ready (a viewer row, an audit insert, the journal appender's read) costs this, or it is load, is not settled: measure web/perf/usable.perf.ts subdomain comment ready on a quiet machine, branch against main, before merging.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1719},"end":{"line":1724},"content_hash":"d7d7999a2c1c93d287ddd23c909a4e8374ad6471e481c1f2e2c68db2057c588b"},"summary":"Time to usable's subdomain comment ready runs over its limit on this branch now and then, never on main","supersedes":"f585f63eb035eabc9a041442847db6819b2b091091ac5b35bf07669c1e8c6e86","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.259348Z","id":"501e7f1dda04d69e636620ec5ea2126629233cd1b0582a734a31c27579405ed3","body":{"detail":"Line 12 says the toolpath-audit design is on branch toolpath-audit, not yet merged; section 20 and M27 say it landed on main with migration 23.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"ac3b777dfe6d4ae3767334718398649c37d62331fb2f48f454d098e8ea5b009f"},"suggested_fix":"Say it is on main (migration 23).","summary":"The header still calls toolpath-audit an unmerged branch","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T15:09:31.206624Z","id":"9673c3b260aae88688c8359ab0b17f22a06724482ce3d31497961b2f91444561","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e423bfb","summary":"Fixed: lines 11-12 now say the toolpath-audit design is on main since migration 23. Evidence: sed -n 11,12p of the spec at e423bfb prints 'Interacts with: `2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md` (on main since / migration 23; §20).'","supersedes":"501e7f1dda04d69e636620ec5ea2126629233cd1b0582a734a31c27579405ed3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
